<html><head><link href='https://aspredicted.org/css/style.css?version_date=1751625322' rel='stylesheet' type='text/css' ><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/3.3.7/css/bootstrap.min.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/5.13.1/css/all.min.css"><script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>
			<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://code.jquery.com/ui/1.12.1/themes/base/jquery-ui.css">
			<script src="https://code.jquery.com/ui/1.12.1/jquery-ui.js"></script><link rel="icon" href="https://aspredicted.org/images/favicon_aspredicted.svg">
		  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="https://aspredicted.org/favicons/apple-touch-icon.png">
			<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="https://aspredicted.org/images/favicons/favicon-32x32.png">
			<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="https://aspredicted.org/images/favicons/favicon-16x16.png">
		<link rel="mask-icon" href="https://aspredicted.org/images/favicons/safari-pinned-tab.svg" color="#5bbad5">
		<meta name="msapplication-TileColor" content="#da532c">
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff">
		</head>

		<body>
			<div class="container-fluid" style="vertical:align:middle">
				<div class="row" style="background-color:#f7f7f7;padding-top:10px">
				<div class="col-md-6">
					<img class="img-responsive logo" src="/images/aspredicted_penn_wharton.png"  style="margin-left:1px;float:left;width:300px">
				</div>
				<div class="col-md-6">
					<a href="http://credlab.wharton.upenn.edu" target="_blank">
					<img class="img-responsive logo" src="https://aspredicted.org/images/CredLab Logo 2020_transparent.svg" style="margin-right:1px;float:right; width:175">
					</a>
				</div>	
			</div>
		</div>	<div class='container' style='width:1400px'><div style='margin-left:20px;margin-right:20px;margin-top:10px;'><a href='https://aspredicted.org'><button class='btn btn_blue btn_topbar'>HOME</button></a></div></div></div><hr></div><div class='container' style='width:900px;font-size:16px'><h3 style='text-align:center'><B>'<i>SNARC effect and temporal stability of finger counting</i>'<BR></B>(AsPredicted #54028)<BR><a href='download_pdf.php?a=ME9qNHdiYjBmb2JlcmNVelZNVm91Zz09&t=VkNJbkg2Y3pucFpoRHhrSzgxa3hydz09'>
							<button class='btn btn_blue'>Download PDF</button>
					   </a></h3><HR><div class='row'><div class='col-md-8'><B>Author(s)</B><BR>Mateusz Hohol (Jagiellonian University) - mateusz.hohol@uj.edu.pl<BR>Kinga Wołoszyn (Jagiellonian University) - kinga.woloszyn@doctoral.uj.edu.pl<BR>Aleksandra Kolny (Jagiellonian University) - ola.kolny@student.uj.edu.pl<BR>Krzyszof Cipora (Loughborough University) - k.cipora@lboro.ac.uk<BR></div><div class='col-md-4' style='text-align:right;'><B>Pre-registered on</b><BR><span style='font-size:85%'>2020/12/10 - 10:49 AM (PT)</span></div></div><HR><B>1) Have any data been collected for this study already?</B><BR>No, no data have been collected for this study yet.<BR><BR><B>2) What's the main question being asked or hypothesis being tested in this study?</B><BR>  Our primary purpose is to investigate the link between the temporal stability of finger counting (FC) routines and the spatial-numerical association of response codes (SNARC effect; in a speeded bimanual decision task, left-to-right readers respond faster to small magnitude numbers with their left hand and to large magnitude numbers with their right hand; Dehaene, Bossini, Giraux, 1993, J. Exp. Psychol. Gen.). According to Fischer (2008, Cortex), FC routines are linked to the SNARC: participants, who start FC from their left hand reveal stronger SNARC than those, who start from their right hand. The latter group is also characterized by larger variation in the SNARC effect. On the other hand, we know that there is a huge variation in stability of FC routines (Hohol et al., 2018, PeerJ). We hypothesize that individuals characterized by stable number-to-finger mappings (measured declaratively; item 1 of the FC questionnaire; Hohol et al., 2018, PeerJ) reveal stronger SNARC effect than individuals, who are unstable in their FC routines. We also hypothesize, following Fischer (2008, Cortex), that stable left-starters should be characterized by stronger SNARC effect than right-starters. We also expect to replicate our previous result that FC routines of the majority of individuals are relatively stable over time (Hohol et al., 2018, PeerJ).<BR><BR><B>3) Describe the key dependent variable(s) specifying how they will be measured.</B><BR>  The key dependent variable is the SNARC effect slope (explained further in the hypothesis and the analyses sections).<BR><BR><B>4) How many and which conditions will participants be assigned to?</B><BR>  In the parity judgment task, there are 3 within-subject conditions: (1) the number presented on a screen can be either even or odd; (2) the number can be either smaller or bigger than 5; (3) the correct response to numbers smaller than 5 might be assigned to left or right hand (for the numbers bigger than 5, respectively).<BR><BR><B>5) Specify exactly which analyses you will conduct to examine the main question/hypothesis.</B><BR>  To compute the SNARC effect, we will apply the Fias, Brysbaert et al.’s (1996, Math. Cogn.) method (used in Cipora, Hohol et al., 2016, Psychol. Res.). dRT (RT right hand - RT left hand) values will be regressed on number magnitude. Non-standardized regression slopes will indicate the SNARC effect. To examine whether there is a significant SNARC effect at the sample level, the slopes will be tested against zero with the one-sample t test. To investigate the relationship between the SNARC effect and temporal stability of finger counting Jonckheere–Terpstra test will be conducted (there are three response options in the stability question, and we expect a monotone decrease in the strength of the SNARC effect with decreasing declared stability of FC routines). In order to compare stable left-starters and stable right-starters t-test will be applied.<BR><BR><B>6) Describe exactly how outliers will be defined and handled, and your precise rule(s) for excluding observations.</B><BR>  From the analyses we will exclude all participants who, in the FC routines questionnaire did not fill questions about FC temporal stability. Regarding the parity judgment task, we will go the same way as in Cipora, Hohol et al., 2016, Psychol. Res. Correct responses with RTs &lt; 200 ms will be considered as anticipations and rejected from further analyses. We will implement a sequential trimming method to cope with the problem of outlier RTs. Mean RTs and SDs will be computed for each participant individually. RTs outside ±3 SD from the participant’s mean will be discarded. Also data from participants with excessive error rates in the parity judgment task will be discarded.<BR><BR><B>7) How many observations will be collected or what will determine sample size?<BR><font size='2'> No need to justify decision, but be precise about <u>exactly</u> how the number will be determined.</font></B><BR>  The planned sample size is 60 adults. The SNARC effect itself is robust, however, a relatively high number of participants is needed to investigate the relationship between the SNARC and FC temporal stability. In the parity judgment task, there will be 480 experimental trials (8 numbers x 30 x 2 blocks).<BR><BR><B>8) Anything else you would like to pre-register? <BR><font size='2'>(e.g., secondary analyses, variables collected for exploratory purposes, unusual analyses planned?)</font></B><BR>  <BR><BR><div style='text-align:right;font-size:70%;color:gray;'>Version of AsPredicted Questions: 2.00</div></div><center><div id='footer' style='margin-bottom:30px;' ><hr><a href='http://credlab.wharton.upenn.edu' target='_blank'><img src='https://aspredicted.org/images/CredLab Logo 2020_transparent.svg' width='165'></a><BR><BR><span style='font-size:small;'><a href='mailto:support@aspredicted.org?subject=I would like to report a bug'>Report a bug</a>  &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href='mailto:support@aspredicted.org?subject=I have a suggestion for ResearchBox'>Make a suggestion</a>  &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href='https://aspredicted.org/terms'>Terms of use</a>       &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href='https://aspredicted.org/help'>Help</a>       &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href='https://aspredicted.org/about'>About</a><BR><BR></center></div></div><script src='https://aspredicted.org/js/shared/main.js?version_date=1752905264' type='text/javascript'></script><script src='https://aspredicted.org/js/footer.js?version_date=1727788481' type='text/javascript'></script>	
